                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Loved this game (I like trains, what can I say), and in my opinion it doesn't need any H-scenes to be a masterpiece. The story contains a lot of train trivia, but there are helpful tips and an entire encyclopedia included so you can brush up on your train knowledge while playing the game. That's not necessary however if it  doesn't interest you, as the most important things are explained in game. Overall however, the story is about a traumatized guy who together with the #1 Raillord of the steam locomotive 8620 and the other girls in his hometown tries to revitalize the train infrastructure in order to bring tourism back and stop a huge corporation from opening a factory which could poison the town's water supply.\nThe story has great emotional depth despite the somewhat dry premise and in my opinion is worth reading for anyone who loves a great story with cute girls (and trains!).\n\nBecause I personally detest cut content, I did research on the R18 patch, but it apparently only adds extra scenes after the story and doesn't actually contribute to the story at all, which is why I skipped it. If you are interested in the full experience however, and can't locate the official patch anymore (the two fan patches for decensoring and removal of mosaics are easily found), my advice would be to check out the Steam group \"Nukige\" or their Discord as they often provide help with locating hard to find VN patches and will likely have the most up-to-date information on where to find it. That's not a guarantee however, as, according to some in the Game Hub, the patch is lost forever (which I personally find hard to believe).\n\nOverall, I would give this VN a 9/10 even with the cut content. It's just too bad the sequel, Maitetsu: Last Run, is only available in Japanese, but if you can fluently speak (or read) the language it is available here on Steam too.",
